  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How you get around",
     "texto": [
      "For means of transport you travel inside, French uses **en** (unlike English «by»): **en bus**, **en train**, **en voiture** (by car), **en métro**. On a bike or on foot, you use **à**: **à vélo** (by bike), **à pied** (on foot). In casual speech you also hear **en vélo**; here we practise the recommended form in careful French: **à vélo**.",
      "With no vehicle inside, you use **à**: **à vélo** (by bike), **à pied** (on foot).",
      "You can also say **Je prends le bus** (I take the bus).",
      "**Comment tu vas au travail ?** = how do you get to work?"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "At the station",
     "texto": [
      "**Un billet pour Lyon** (a ticket for Lyon).",
      "**Aller simple** = one-way. **Aller-retour** = return.",
      "**Le train part à quelle heure ?** (what time does the train leave?). It leaves from a **quai** (platform).",
      "For duration: **Ça dure combien de temps ?** (how long does it last?). **Environ** = about."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reading a timetable",
     "texto": [
      "At a station, **destination** shows where the train goes, **départ** the departure time and **quai** the platform. First find your destination, then read the details in that row."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
